// This suite locks in the fallback ROUTING behavior, not just "recognized
// vs unknown" like the vocabulary batches — each case asserts the SPECIFIC
// fallback category Coach must land in (out-of-scope, no-verified-data,
// personal-assistant, capability-limit, clarification, or genuine unknown),
// and separately asserts the hard requirement: false event matches = 0.
//
// Candidates were generated combinatorially across categories (weather,
// sports, trivia, shopping, personal-advice, food, movies, politics,
// finance, games, schoolwork for OUT_OF_SCOPE; a dedicated negative corpus
// of ordinary words that must never resolve to a TSA event; personal
// questions about the assistant; capability-limit asks; TSA-related
// questions with no verified answer; and clarification-needed asks), then
// swept against the real engine to confirm each one lands in its intended
// category. See the methodology note at the end of this file for full
// metrics (generated/passing counts per category, false-event-match count).

